/div><h3 class=3D"TextBase-hXhSqg Title-HRvkwB" data-d-text-flow=3D"" data-=
d-component=3D"title" data-d-size=3D"md" data-d-weight=3D"semibold">The one=
-minute explanation to remember</h3><p class=3D"TextBase-hXhSqg Text-lIMP0_=
" data-d-text-flow=3D"" data-d-component=3D"text">Lex reads the input and c=
onverts source-code characters into tokens. YACC receives those tokens thro=
ugh <code class=3D"Code-kbs71c" data-d-component=3D"code">yylex()</code> an=
d checks them against grammar rules defined in <code class=3D"Code-kbs71c" =
data-d-component=3D"code">parser.y</code>. The grammar describes the struct=
ure of a <code class=3D"Code-kbs71c" data-d-component=3D"code">for</code> l=
oop, including initialization, condition, update, statements and expression=
s. If the input follows the grammar, <code class=3D"Code-kbs71c" data-d-com=
ponent=3D"code">yyparse()</code> returns <code class=3D"Code-kbs71c" data-d=
-component=3D"code">0</code>; otherwise, it reports a syntax error through =
<code class=3D"Code-kbs71c" data-d-component=3D"code">yyerror()</code>.</p>=
